==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|finstar}}, which probably dissimilated from {{m|goh|dinstar}}, making it a descendant of {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*þiustrijaz||dark, without light}}. Cognates with {{cog|nl|duister||dark}}, {{cog|en|thester||dark}}, {{cog|de|finster||dark}}.

